Third-party material
--------------------

Runtime dependency
  @modelcontextprotocol/client 2.2.0 — MIT, the Model Context Protocol project.
  It is used unmodified as the MCP wire client for the stdio, Streamable HTTP
  and SSE transports.

Peer dependency
  The package declares a single peer dependency on @deepseek-ai/cordis, which the
  DeepSeek Harness installation supplies. No @deepseek-ai/* module is imported or
  vendored at runtime; every Harness capability is reached through the Cordis
  context object.

Adapted behavior
  Portions of the MCP connection lifecycle (connect / initialize / tools-list,
  reconnection with backoff, per-server instructions) and of the tool-result
  projection (text in block order, resource links rendered as text, image and
  unsupported-content diagnostics) are adapted from
  @deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client 0.2.1-rc.5, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek
  (DeepSeek Harness). The code in this package is a smaller reimplementation
  for its one-connection-per-server, per-preset model. It does not import or
  vendor that package: a profile-installed plugin cannot resolve Harness
  internal packages, which is also why the tool definition is built by hand
  instead of importing the Harness tool helpers (see
  docs/adr/0005-hand-built-tool-definition.md).

Borrowed patterns
  The bundle patch layout, the Host/Client split, the plugin-owned JSON store
  with atomic replace, and the maintenance CLI follow the ds-hu sibling plugins
  (MIT), notably @ds-hu/dsh-auto-task-center. Those packages are not
  dependencies and their source is not vendored here.

Original material
  The icon (icon.svg), the client UI, and the zh/en locale dictionaries were
  written for this project. "DeepSeek" and "DeepSeek Harness" are names of the
  host platform, not a claim of endorsement.
